    "Use the same effective configuration in native Query API, CLI, request, external Query Work, artifact-scope query seeds and productive validation gates.",
    "Keep original artifact identities and source bytes; hide excluded nodes and edges from computed query graph traversal while checking the full structural inventory.",
    "Reject unknown configuration identities and changed inputs at final observation checks; retain read-only behavior and portable Query execution.",
    "Compare native Query, validation and seed configuration bindings, and derive equal real scope roots from equal verified input/descriptor/provider observations.",
    "Reject invalid selections, stale source files and forged cached source identities; preserve concurrent variant isolation and original metadata contracts when no selection is supplied.",
    "11.l.W: select actual configured rows and eligible graph nodes through the same native Query service, compare stable ID ties and explicit ID ordering, and bind selected scope/configuration plus original bytes. Preserve all potential variants when no selection is supplied.",
